---
export const prerender = false;
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getAllSiteSettings } from '../lib/queries';

const settings = await getAllSiteSettings();
const settingsList = Array.isArray(settings) ? settings : [];
const settingsObj = settingsList.reduce((acc: any, s: any) => { if (s && s.key) acc[s.key] = s.value; return acc; }, {} as Record<string, string>);
const customTerms = settingsObj.terms_custom_text || '';
---

<Layout title="Terms & Conditions - Orandus" description="Terms and conditions for using Orandus.">
  <section class="min-h-screen bg-nitkkr-cream py-12 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto bg-white rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-10 border border-amber-200/80 shadow-sm space-y-6">
      <div>
        <h1 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-nitkkr-dark">📜 Terms & Conditions</h1>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-1">Last updated: September 2026</p>
      </div>

      {customTerms ? (
        <div class="p-4 bg-amber-50 rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-800 leading-relaxed whitespace-pre-line">
          {customTerms}
        </div>
      ) : null}

      <div class="space-y-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">1. What Orandus Actually Is</h2>
          <p>Orandus is a food discovery platform — we help you find food spots, check menus, see prices, and contact vendors directly. That's it.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">We're <strong>not</strong> a delivery app, not a restaurant, not a payment processor. We don't cook, we don't deliver, we don't take orders, we don't process payments. Zero commissions. Zero markups. Zero middleman drama.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">2. Your Transaction = Your Business</h2>
          <p>When you order food, you're dealing directly with the vendor. Price, quantity, payment, delivery, pickup, prep time, cancellations, refunds, replacements, complaints, food quality — that's 100% between you and them.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">Orandus just introduced you. We're not a party to your transaction. We don't guarantee the vendor accepts your order, has the item, delivers on time, or that the food tastes good.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">3. Menu Info = Best Effort, Not a Guarantee</h2>
          <p>We try to keep menus, prices, and hours accurate. But vendors change stuff without telling us. Prices go up, items sell out, timings shift, spots close temporarily.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">Always double-check with the vendor before you trek across campus or place an order. Orandus shows what we know — not a promise.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">4. Reviews: Keep It Real, Keep It Respectful</h2>
          <p>Reviews are public. Other students see your display name and what you wrote.</p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 space-y-1">
            <li>Be honest — fake reviews help no one</li>
            <li>Be respectful — abusive, spammy, or defamatory content gets removed</li>
            <li>Don't put personal info (phone, address, etc.) in reviews</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-2">We moderate. If it crosses the line, it's gone.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">5. Your Content, Your Responsibility</h2>
          <p>If you submit a review, feedback, or correction, you own it. You're responsible for what you post. Don't submit anything illegal, offensive, or that violates someone's rights.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">By submitting, you give us permission to display, store, and moderate it on the platform.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">6. Want Your Review Removed?</h2>
          <p>No problem. Hit up our <a href="/contact" class="text-nitkkr-orange font-bold hover:underline">Contact page</a> and tell us which one. We'll sort it.</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">We may keep minimal records to prevent abuse or resolve disputes.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">7. Vendor Info on Orandus</h2>
          <p>We display vendor names, menus, prices, photos, categories, locations, hours, contact info, and descriptions. Some comes directly from vendors, some from public sources, some we verify ourselves.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">If you're a vendor and something's wrong — <a href="/contact" class="text-nitkkr-orange font-bold hover:underline">tell us</a>. We'll verify and fix it.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">8. External Links = Not Our Circus</h2>
          <p>Orandus links to WhatsApp, phone dialer, maps, Instagram, vendor sites. Once you tap out, their rules apply. We don't control their privacy, security, content, or availability.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">9. No Account, No Passwords (For Now)</h2>
          <p>You don't need an account to browse. No login, no password database for regular users. If that changes, we'll update this.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">10. We Might Add Features Later</h2>
          <p>Vendor dashboards, saved spots, ordering tools, personalized recommendations — if we add stuff that changes how things work, we'll update these terms first.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">11. Site Might Go Down Sometimes</h2>
          <p>Maintenance, tech issues, hosting problems, security incidents — stuff happens. We don't guarantee 24/7 uptime.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">12. We Can Update These Terms</h2>
          <p>When services, tech, or laws change, we'll update this page and the "Last updated" date. If it's a big change, we'll give you a heads up.</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500">Keep checking back occasionally.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">13. The TL;DR</h2>
          <p>Orandus helps you discover food. It doesn't become the seller. The vendor is responsible for their food/service. You're responsible for your decisions.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">14. Contact Us</h2>
          <p>Questions about these terms? <a href="/contact" class="text-nitkkr-orange font-bold hover:underline">Drop us a line</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>